// Inside a MODULE, a function may still use an import alias's name as a variable
// of its own: the function is its own strong environment (MEM-7, GLB-070), and
// there `g` is the local and `g::uno()` the module.
//
// `alias_shadowed_by_variable.zy` is the same rule in a program. In a module the
// web interpreter's checker took everything at module scope for module state,
// aliases included, and refused `m.zy` with "'g' is a module, not a value" — which
// kept GoL from starting in the browser (BUG-VMJS-006, found by the JavaScript
// port of the VM).

<# ./vmjs/m => m
>> m::f(3) ¶
